          },
          "id": "1778621235096",
          "code": "DEFAULT_ACCOUNTIDS_VAR",
          "type": "SET_FIELDS",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778621235096_pAccountIds",
              "name": "pAccountIds",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.accountIds}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Build the ElasticSearch query payload for looking up account PartyId values from comma-separated accountNumbers.",
            "name": "PREPARE_ES_PAYLOAD",
            "language": "JAVASCRIPT",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let accountNumbers = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.accountNumbers;\n\nlet accountNumberValues = String(accountNumbers)\n  .split(',')\n  .map(function (accountNumber) {\n    return accountNumber.trim();\n  })\n  .filter(function (accountNumber) {\n    return accountNumber !== '';\n  });\n\nlet q = {\n  op: '$in',\n  attribute: 'PartyNumber',\n  values: accountNumberValues\n};\n\nlet qStr = JSON.stringify(q);\nreturn qStr;"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8503.5,
            "y": 6132
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778621621600"
          },
          "id": "1778621503058",
          "code": "PREPARE_ES_PAYLOAD",
          "type": "CODE",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Generate SQL filter and sort parameters from the user question and selected query profile.",
            "name": "PROCESS_FILTER_PARAMS",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            }
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7603.5,
            "y": 6354
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778274756497"
          },
          "id": "1778273066331",
          "code": "PROCESS_FILTER_PARAMS",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778273066331_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Task\n\nGenerate SQL filter and sort parameter values for the user question.\n\n# Inputs\n\nqueryProfile: {{$context.$nodes.MAP_ACTION_TO_QUERY_PROFILE.$output.result}}\nqueryIntent: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.queryIntent}}\n\n`queryIntent` may be missing, null, blank, or whitespace.\n\n# Policy\n\nUse `queryProfile` to choose the output shape and field catalog.\n\nIf the user question does not explicitly ask for expired subscriptions or expired/ended installed-base assets, preserve the default active-record filter.\n\nDo not generate filters or sort expressions on identifier fields. ID fields may be returned by the query payload, but they are not valid for generated filtering or sorting.\n\n# Output Contract\n\nReturn valid JSON only. Do not include markdown, comments, or explanatory text.\n\nFor aggregate query profiles, return exactly:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"subscriptions\": {\n    \"preAggregationFilter\": \"s.statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')\",\n    \"postAggregationFilter\": \"1=1\",\n    \"orderBy\": \"totalValueAmount DESC\"\n  },\n  \"installedBase\": {\n    \"preAggregationFilter\": \"(a.endDate IS NULL OR a.endDate >= SYSDATE)\",\n    \"postAggregationFilter\": \"1=1\",\n    \"orderBy\": \"totalValueAmount DESC\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFor `subscriptionDetail`, return only:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"subscriptions\": {\n    \"recordFilter\": \"statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')\",\n    \"orderBy\": \"valueAmount DESC\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFor `installedBaseDetail`, return only:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"installedBase\": {\n    \"recordFilter\": \"(endDate IS NULL OR endDate >= SYSDATE)\",\n    \"orderBy\": \"valueAmount DESC\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDo not return top-level filter or sort keys.\n\nFor aggregate query profiles, decide whether the user intent applies to subscriptions, installed base, or both.\n\n- If the user asks only about subscriptions, set `installedBase.preAggregationFilter` to `1=0`.\n- If the user asks only about installed-base assets, set `subscriptions.preAggregationFilter` to `1=0`.\n- If the user asks about both or the intent is ambiguous, keep both branches active.\n\nExamples:\n- \"subs expiring in 60 days\" is subscription-only, so set `installedBase.preAggregationFilter` to `1=0`.\n- \"assets expiring in 90 days\" is installed-base-only, so set `subscriptions.preAggregationFilter` to `1=0`.\n\nUse `1=1` only when no non-status filter is needed in `postAggregationFilter`.\n\nIf `queryIntent` is missing, null, blank, or whitespace, return the default JSON for the selected `queryProfile`.\n\n# Default Active Filters\n\nUnless the user explicitly asks otherwise, always include these filters:\n\n| Scope | Filter |\n| --- | --- |\n| Subscription detail | `statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')` |\n| Subscription aggregate | `s.statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')` |\n| Installed-base detail | `(endDate IS NULL OR endDate >= SYSDATE)` |\n| Installed-base aggregate | `(a.endDate IS NULL OR a.endDate >= SYSDATE)` |\n\nWhen adding query-intent filters, combine them with the default active filter using `AND`. The generated query-intent filter must narrow the default active result set; it must not replace or drop the active filter unless the user explicitly asks for expired subscriptions or expired/ended installed-base assets.\n\nExamples:\n- Active installed-base assets with value over 10000: `(endDate IS NULL OR endDate >= SYSDATE) AND valueAmount > 10000`\n- Active subscriptions expiring in the next 90 days: `statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT') AND nextRenewalDate >= TRUNC(SYSDATE) AND nextRenewalDate < TRUNC(SYSDATE) + 90`\n- Expired installed-base assets with value over 10000: `endDate < SYSDATE AND valueAmount > 10000`\n- Expired subscriptions for coverage products: `statusCode = 'ORA_EXPIRED' AND salesProductTypeCode = 'COVERAGE'`\n\n# Subscription Status Rules\n\nOnly support active subscriptions and expired subscriptions.\n\n| User wording | Detail filter | Aggregate filter |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| active subscriptions, current subscriptions, live subscriptions | `statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')` | `s.statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')` |\n| expired subscriptions | `statusCode = 'ORA_EXPIRED'` | `s.statusCode = 'ORA_EXPIRED'` |\n\nRules:\n- If the user does not explicitly ask for expired subscriptions, use the active subscription filter.\n- If the user explicitly asks for expired subscriptions, use only `ORA_EXPIRED` and do not include the active subscription filter.\n- Do not generate filters for canceled, closed, draft, pending approval, suspended, or any other subscription statuses.\n\n# Installed-Base Status Rules\n\nInstalled-base activity is determined by `endDate`.\n\n| User wording | Detail filter | Aggregate filter |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| active assets, current assets, installed assets | `(endDate IS NULL OR endDate >= SYSDATE)` | `(a.endDate IS NULL OR a.endDate >= SYSDATE)` |\n| expired assets, ended assets, assets past end date | `endDate < SYSDATE` | `a.endDate < SYSDATE` |\n\nIf the user does not explicitly ask for expired or ended assets, use the active installed-base filter.\n\n# SQL Rules\n\n- Use only fields listed in the selected `queryProfile` catalog.\n- Do not add, remove, or change field aliases.\n- Do not include `WHERE` or `ORDER BY`.\n- Use a field only in the parameter scope where it is listed.\n- Fields scoped to `preAggregationFilter` may be used only in `preAggregationFilter`.\n- Fields scoped to `postAggregationFilter` may be used only in `postAggregationFilter` and `orderBy`.\n- Fields scoped to `recordFilter` may be used only in `recordFilter` and `orderBy`.\n- For aggregate query profiles, subscription fields may be used only under `subscriptions`, and installed-base fields may be used only under `installedBase`.\n- Use single quotes for string literals.\n- Use `LIKE` for partial text matching.\n- Use `IN (...)` for multiple explicit values.\n- Use `IS NULL` and `IS NOT NULL` for null checks.\n- Do not compare to `null` using `=`.\n- Use `TO_DATE('YYYY-MM-DD','YYYY-MM-DD')` for literal date comparisons.\n- Use `ADD_MONTHS(TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM'), n)` for calendar-month windows.\n- Use `TRUNC(SYSDATE) + n` for rolling-day windows.\n- Do not invent fields, aliases, joins, subqueries, functions, or tables.\n- Do not generate filters or sort expressions using identifier fields such as `itemId`, `productCategoryId`, `productGroupId`, `productHierarchyId`, `accountId`, `subscriptionId`, `subscriptionProductId`, or `assetId`.\n- Use name or number fields instead of ID fields for natural-language product, category, hierarchy, subscription, or asset queries.\n\n# Field Type Rules\n\n- `string`: use `=`, `IN (...)`, or `LIKE`.\n- `number`: use numeric comparison operators such as `=`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`.\n- `date`: use date comparisons, `IS NULL`, or `IS NOT NULL`.\n- `currency number`: use numeric comparison operators. Values are already in corporate currency where the description says so.\n\n# Product Type Values\n\nUse these values only when `salesProductTypeCode` is available in the selected field catalog.\n\n| User wording | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| subscriptions, subscription products, SaaS subscriptions, subscription revenue | `'SUBSCRIPTION'` |\n| coverage, support coverage, extended warranty, warranty products | `'COVERAGE'` |\n\n# aggregateByProductHierarchy\n\nUse this catalog when `queryProfile` is `aggregateByProductHierarchy`.\n\n## preAggregationFilter Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Data family | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `s.statusCode` | string | Subscription | Subscription status code. Use only for active or expired subscription filtering. |\n| `s.salesProductTypeCode` | string | Subscription | Product type code, such as subscription or coverage. |\n| `s.startDate` | date | Subscription | Subscription product start date before aggregation. |\n| `s.endDate` | date | Subscription | Subscription product end date before aggregation. |\n| `r.nextRenewalDate` | date | Subscription | Next subscription renewal date before aggregation. Use for renewal timing. |\n| `s.netPriceInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Subscription net price, contract value, TCV, spend, or value before aggregation. |\n| `s.mrrInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Monthly recurring revenue before aggregation. |\n| `s.arrInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Annual recurring revenue before aggregation. |\n| `s.productGroupName` | string | Subscription | Product hierarchy group name used for hierarchy grouping. |\n| `s.productCategoryName` | string | Subscription | Product category name. |\n| `a.startDate` | date | Installed Base | Installed-base asset start date before aggregation. |\n| `a.endDate` | date | Installed Base | Installed-base asset end date before aggregation. Use for expiration, ending, or refresh timing. |\n| `a.valueAmountInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Installed Base | Installed-base asset value before aggregation. |\n| `a.productGroupName` | string | Installed Base | Product hierarchy group name used for hierarchy grouping. |\n| `a.productCategoryName` | string | Installed Base | Product category name. |\n\n## postAggregationFilter And orderBy Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Data family | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `productGroupName` | string | Shared | Grouped product hierarchy group name. |\n| `productCategoryName` | string | Shared | Product category name. |\n| `totalValueAmount` | currency number | Shared | Aggregated total value, spend, contract value, or installed-base value. |\n| `totalMRR` | currency number | Subscription | Aggregated monthly recurring revenue. Do not use for installed base. |\n| `totalARR` | currency number | Subscription | Aggregated annual recurring revenue. Do not use for installed base. |\n\nDefault `orderBy`: `totalValueAmount DESC`\n\n# aggregateByProduct\n\nUse this catalog when `queryProfile` is `aggregateByProduct`.\n\n## preAggregationFilter Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Data family | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `s.itemNumber` | string | Subscription | Subscription product item number before aggregation. |\n| `s.itemName` | string | Subscription | Subscription product item name before aggregation. Use for product text search. |\n| `s.statusCode` | string | Subscription | Subscription status code. Use only for active or expired subscription filtering. |\n| `s.salesProductTypeCode` | string | Subscription | Product type code, such as subscription or coverage. |\n| `s.startDate` | date | Subscription | Subscription product start date before aggregation. |\n| `s.endDate` | date | Subscription | Subscription product end date before aggregation. |\n| `r.nextRenewalDate` | date | Subscription | Next subscription renewal date before aggregation. Use for renewal timing. |\n| `s.netPriceInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Subscription net price, contract value, TCV, spend, or value before aggregation. |\n| `s.mrrInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Monthly recurring revenue before aggregation. |\n| `s.arrInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Subscription | Annual recurring revenue before aggregation. |\n| `s.productCategoryName` | string | Subscription | Product category name. |\n| `a.itemNumber` | string | Installed Base | Installed-base asset item number before aggregation. |\n| `a.itemName` | string | Installed Base | Installed-base asset item name before aggregation. Use for product text search. |\n| `a.startDate` | date | Installed Base | Installed-base asset start date before aggregation. |\n| `a.endDate` | date | Installed Base | Installed-base asset end date before aggregation. Use for expiration, ending, or refresh timing. |\n| `a.valueAmountInCorporateCurrency` | currency number | Installed Base | Installed-base asset value before aggregation. |\n| `a.productCategoryName` | string | Installed Base | Product category name. |\n\n## postAggregationFilter And orderBy Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Data family | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `itemNumber` | string | Shared | Product item number. |\n| `itemName` | string | Shared | Product item name. |\n| `productCategoryName` | string | Shared | Product category name. |\n| `earliestEndDate` | date | Installed Base | Earliest installed-base end date in the grouped result. Do not use for subscription. |\n| `totalValueAmount` | currency number | Shared | Aggregated total value, spend, contract value, or installed-base value. |\n| `totalMRR` | currency number | Subscription | Aggregated monthly recurring revenue. Do not use for installed base. |\n| `totalARR` | currency number | Subscription | Aggregated annual recurring revenue. Do not use for installed base. |\n\nDefault `orderBy`: `totalValueAmount DESC`\n\n# subscriptionDetail\n\nUse this catalog when `queryProfile` is `subscriptionDetail`.\n\n## recordFilter And orderBy Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `itemNumber` | string | Subscription product item number. |\n| `itemName` | string | Subscription product item name. Use for product text search. |\n| `statusCode` | string | Subscription status code. Use only for active or expired subscription filtering. |\n| `salesProductTypeCode` | string | Product type code, such as subscription or coverage. |\n| `productCategoryName` | string | Product category name. |\n| `startDate` | date | Subscription product start date. |\n| `endDate` | date | Subscription product end date. |\n| `nextRenewalDate` | date | Next subscription renewal date. Use for renewal timing. |\n| `valueAmount` | currency number | Subscription value, net price, contract value, TCV, or spend. |\n| `mrr` | currency number | Monthly recurring revenue. |\n| `arr` | currency number | Annual recurring revenue. |\n\nDefault `orderBy`: `valueAmount DESC`\n\n# installedBaseDetail\n\nUse this catalog when `queryProfile` is `installedBaseDetail`.\n\n## recordFilter And orderBy Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `itemNumber` | string | Installed-base asset item number. |\n| `itemName` | string | Installed-base asset item name. Use for product text search. |\n| `productCategoryName` | string | Product category name. |\n| `startDate` | date | Installed-base asset start date. |\n| `endDate` | date | Installed-base asset end date. Use for expiration, ending, or refresh timing. |\n| `installedDate` | date | Installed date for the asset. |\n| `purchaseDate` | date | Purchase date for the asset. |\n| `valueAmount` | currency number | Installed-base asset value. |\n\nDefault `orderBy`: `valueAmount DESC`\n\n# Date Window Patterns\n\nFor next calendar month, use:\n\n```sql\n<dateField> >= ADD_MONTHS(TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM'), 1)\nAND <dateField> < ADD_MONTHS(TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM'), 2)\n```\n\nFor next N rolling days, use:\n\n```sql\n<dateField> >= TRUNC(SYSDATE)\nAND <dateField> < TRUNC(SYSDATE) + N\n```\n\n# Final Output\n\nUse `queryProfile` and `queryIntent` to generate the filter JSON.\n\nIf `queryIntent` is missing, null, blank, or whitespace, return the default JSON for the selected `queryProfile`.\n\nIf `queryIntent` is present, preserve the default active-record filter unless the user explicitly asks for expired subscriptions or expired/ended installed-base assets.\n\nReturn only valid JSON.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": true\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1778532074372",
          "code": "DEFAULT_QUERY_PROFILE",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Returns the default filter and ordering object for the resolved query profile, matching the shape expected by downstream aggregate and detail business-object calls.",
            "name": "DEFAULT_QUERY_PROFILE",
            "sourceCode": "var queryProfile = $context.$nodes.MAP_ACTION_TO_QUERY_PROFILE.$output.result;\n\nif (queryProfile === 'subscriptionDetail') {\n  return {\n    subscriptions: {\n      recordFilter: \"statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')\",\n      orderBy: 'valueAmount DESC'\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nif (queryProfile === 'installedBaseDetail') {\n  return {\n    installedBase: {\n      recordFilter: '(endDate IS NULL OR endDate >= SYSDATE)',\n      orderBy: 'valueAmount DESC'\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nif (\n  queryProfile === 'aggregateByProductHierarchy' ||\n  queryProfile === 'aggregateByProduct'\n) {\n  return {\n    subscriptions: {\n      preAggregationFilter: \"s.statusCode IN ('ORA_ACTIVE', 'ORA_HOLD', 'ORA_UNDER_AMENDMENT')\",\n      postAggregationFilter: '1=1',\n      orderBy: 'totalValueAmount DESC'\n    },\n    installedBase: {\n      preAggregationFilter: '(a.endDate IS NULL OR a.endDate >= SYSDATE)',\n      postAggregationFilter: '1=1',\n      orderBy: 'totalValueAmount DESC'\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nthrow new Error('Unsupported queryProfile: ' + queryProfile);\n",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8053.5,
            "y": 6354
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778274536250"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
